course: dictionary
lesson: 9555
title: One word, many storms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word storm can mean different things. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning you need. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The storm knocked down trees and cut the power.» Here a storm is very bad weather with strong winds and often heavy rain. Trees falling and the power going off are the clues.
explain: «The crowd gave a storm of clapping.» Clapping cannot blow down a tree, so this storm is a sudden show of strong feeling. Try the swap: "a sudden show of clapping" still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: «She stormed out of the room.» Here storm is a verb, and it means to go somewhere quickly and angrily. Check it by swapping in "left quickly and angrily": the sentence still works.
fact: Storm can be a noun (a storm, storms) or a verb (storm, stormed, storming).
fact: A storm is very bad weather with strong winds and often heavy rain, snow, hail, thunder and lightning.
fact: Types of storm include thunderstorms, snowstorms (blizzards), hurricanes, cyclones, typhoons, tornadoes and dust storms.
fact: During a storm, stay indoors, away from windows and water, and never shelter under trees.
fact: «A storm in a teacup» means a big fuss about something small.
exercise: «The storm knocked down trees and cut the power.» What does storm mean? | To go somewhere quickly and angrily | A sudden show of strong feeling | To attack a place suddenly | * Very bad weather with strong winds
exercise: «She stormed out of the room.» What does stormed mean? | * Left quickly and angrily | Sat down quietly | Fell asleep | Rained heavily
exercise: «The crowd gave a storm of clapping.» What does storm mean here? | Very bad weather | * A sudden show of strong feeling | A type of cloud | To attack a place suddenly
test: «The soldiers stormed the castle at dawn.» What does stormed mean? | * Attacked the place suddenly | Painted the walls | Cleaned the castle | Quietly left the castle
test: Which of these is a type of storm? | Rainbow | * Blizzard | Sunbeam | Breeze
exam: Which sentence uses storm as a verb? | The storm hit at night | Storm clouds grew dark over the hills | * He stormed off in a temper | A storm of rain fell on the roof
